- `old` MUST be a substring that appears exactly once in the file.
- `new` is the same text plus your change.
- You do NOT need to provide the whole file.
- If your first edit fails with "old not found", pick a smaller/more unique
  snippet and try again. Do not retry the identical edit.

### 5. Validate (light — do not block on this)

If the file you changed has a `workflow_dispatch:` trigger with a `task` input,
you MUST pass `-f task=...` or GitHub rejects with HTTP 422:

    gh(["workflow","run","deepseek-termux-agent.yml",
        "--repo","timerloggedout-spec/termux-monorepo","--ref","master",
        "-f","task=validation ping from agent"])
    run(["sleep","15"])
    gh(["run","list","--repo","timerloggedout-spec/termux-monorepo",
        "--workflow","deepseek-termux-agent.yml","--limit","1",
        "--json","status,conclusion"])

If the workflow has no `task` input, plain dispatch is fine.

Mark `"validation":"deferred"` with reason `"non-behavioral change — failure-path only"`
if the change only affects an `if: failure()` path that cannot be exercised without
a real failure. That is a valid and honest outcome.

### 6. Sync + finish
    logs_sync()
    finish(summary='{"file":"...","change":"...","commit":"...","validation":"passed|deferred"}')

## Forbidden
- `run` with sh/bash/base64/curl/mkdir — not allowlisted. Do not try.
- Piping tool output through shell. No `|`.
- Retrying the same failing tool call more than twice.

## On failure
If your 3rd attempt at gh_edit_file fails, call finish with
validation="deferred" and a one-line reason. That is a valid outcome.

